{
  "uid": "sightline-tenants",
  "title": "Sightline — customers and onboarding",
  "description": "Who gets through onboarding, where they fall out, and what the limits turn away. What the agent costs is on 'Sightline — the agent'.",
  "tags": ["sightline"],
  "timezone": "browser",
  "schemaVersion": 39,
  "version": 1,
  "editable": true,
  "refresh": "5m",
  "time": {
    "from": "now-7d",
    "to": "now"
  },
  "panels": [
    {
      "id": 1,
      "title": "Connections by status",
      "type": "timeseries",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 7,
        "w": 8,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 0
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "Prometheus"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "Prometheus"
          },
          "expr": "sum by (status) (sightline_connections)",
          "legendFormat": "{{status}}"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "custom": {}
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "description": "The funnel as a gauge. pending that never becomes verified is somebody who gave up partway through onboarding."
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "title": "Onboarding failures by cause (24h)",
      "type": "timeseries",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 7,
        "w": 8,
        "x": 8,
        "y": 0
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "Prometheus"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "Prometheus"
          },
          "expr": "sum by (reason) (increase(sightline_assume_role_failures_total[24h]))",
          "legendFormat": "{{reason}}"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "custom": {},
          "noValue": "None in this window"
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "description": "diagnose() has already reduced an AccessDenied to which of three things it is. If one cause dominates, the instructions are wrong rather than the customers."
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "title": "Time to verify a connection",
      "type": "timeseries",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 7,
        "w": 8,
        "x": 16,
        "y": 0
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "Prometheus"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "Prometheus"
          },
          "expr": "histogram_quantile(0.95, sum by (le, outcome) (rate(sightline_connection_verify_duration_seconds_bucket[6h])))",
          "legendFormat": "p95 {{outcome}}"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "custom": {},
          "unit": "s",
          "noValue": "None in this window"
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "description": "How long the Connect screen sits amber. Minutes here is the difference between finishing onboarding and abandoning it."
    },
    {
      "id": 8,
      "title": "Requests a limit refused (6h)",
      "type": "timeseries",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 7,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 7
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "Prometheus"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "Prometheus"
          },
          "expr": "sum by (kind, what) (increase(sightline_requests_refused_total[6h]))",
          "legendFormat": "{{what}} — {{kind}}"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "custom": {},
          "noValue": "None in this window"
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "description": "throttled is the caller's own usage catching up; paused is an operator having turned something off. The two mean entirely different things and only one is a problem."
    },
    {
      "id": 9,
      "title": "Requests that named no account",
      "type": "timeseries",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 7,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 12,
        "y": 7
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "Prometheus"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "Prometheus"
          },
          "expr": "rate(sightline_requests_without_connection_header_total[30m]) * 1800",
          "legendFormat": "per 30m"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "custom": {}
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "description": "The fallback to the tenant's oldest connection is safe but it is also what made two resource panels answer about the wrong AWS account. A number climbing here means a client stopped sending the header."
    }
  ],
  "links": [
    {
      "type": "dashboards",
      "tags": ["sightline"],
      "asDropdown": false,
      "title": "Sightline",
      "includeVars": false,
      "keepTime": true
    }
  ]
}
